Z||000000||Firebug||06-05-2001||07:25 PM||||I am converting my car from a 4 cyl to a v-6.  What must I replace as far as fuel lines go.  The V-6 that I have is missing everything after the fuel rail.  The Fiero has all of it's 4 cyl. fuel lines intact.  I believe that I have to replace all of the lines from the fuel tank on.  I would just like to hear from people that have done this.  <P>Thanks, <BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierokid87||06-06-2001||01:21 AM||||Ok what year is your car?  Cuzz if its an 87 or and 88 you dont have to change the fuel lines, as they are the same from the 4 cyld to the V-6.  Im doing the same conversion 4 cyld to V-6 and I found out the only thing under the car I have to change is the fuel pump.  The coolant pipe on the Driverside I only have to cut.<P>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/sfiero/Mybaby.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000002||Firebug||06-06-2001||08:34 PM||||I have an '85 and I have none of the fuel lines from the V-6.  All I have is two holes in the fuel rail.  <P>Thanks, <BR>Scott||||reg||1
Z||000003||DandRauto||06-06-2001||10:51 PM||||Fierokid87.<P>Why and where do you cut the cooling line.  Also, you said that none of the fuel lines need to be changed?  What is the source of info, I thought that because of the increase presure that they need to be up-graded||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierokid87||06-07-2001||12:25 AM||||Onthe 87-88 Fieros the Fuel lines are the same.  They come up in the same area and they follow the same rout.  Even the coolant line are the same accept where the driver side one turns up to go to the V-6 on the 4 cyld it make two more bends.  My sourse of infor is Ed parks.  and myself.  since Ive looked closly at the V-6 and the 4 cyld set ups<P>Scott||||reg||1
